
# FilmLog — Ionic Mobile App (v1)

A mobile movie discovery and personal tracking application built with Ionic and Angular, modelled after apps like Letterboxd and IMDb. Built for INF 354 Assignment 2 at the University of Pretoria.

## What It Does

- **Authentication** — simulated login/signup using local storage
- **Movie Search** — searches real movies via the live IMDb API
- **Watchlist** — add movies you plan to watch, stored locally with Ionic Storage
- **Watched List** — mark movies as watched, track how many times you've seen them, and reset the counter
- **Movie Details** — view title, release year, cast, and poster for any selected movie

## Tech Stack

- Ionic (Angular)
- Angular (`HttpClient` for API calls)
- TypeScript
- Ionic Storage (local database)
- IMDb API (`https://imdb.iamidiotareyoutoo.com`)
- SCSS

## Pages / Navigation

| Page | Description |
|------|-------------|
| Login / Register | Simulated auth with local storage |
| Search | Search movies live from IMDb API, displayed in Ionic List |
| Movie Details | Title, year, cast, poster — Add to Watchlist or Mark as Watched |
| Watchlist | All movies the user wants to watch; removable |
| Watched | All watched movies; removable, with times-watched counter and reset button |

Navigation implemented via Ionic tab bar (Search / Watchlist / Watched).

## How to Run

**Prerequisites:** Node.js, Ionic CLI (`npm install -g @ionic/cli`)

```bash
cd filmlog-ionic
npm install
ionic serve
```

The app opens in your browser simulating a mobile device. For a native device preview use:
```bash
ionic serve --lab
```

## What I Learned

- Building a multi-page Ionic/Angular mobile application
- Consuming a live external REST API with Angular's `HttpClient`
- Persisting user data locally with Ionic Storage
- Implementing tab-based navigation in Ionic
- Managing state across pages (moving movies between Watchlist and Watched List)
- Simulating authentication with local storage
